{
  "conventions": [
    {
      "source": "CLAUDE.md",
      "rule": "Every changed line must trace to the request — no opportunistic refactors of adjacent code or unrelated formatting"
    },
    {
      "source": "CLAUDE.md",
      "rule": "§11.3: organize docs/ as numbered chapters in reading order (NN-topic.md), matching the README Documentation table order — a new/renamed doc entry must stay consistent with both"
    },
    {
      "source": "CLAUDE.md",
      "rule": "§16: no ad-hoc planning/implementation — planning itself is mandated to go through Skill(autopilot:plan); §15 git workflow mandates route branch/commit/PR/issue creation through the autopilot:* skills, never raw git/gh"
    },
    {
      "source": "docs/05-plan-run-skills.md",
      "rule": "\"The plan file is output, not instructions\": no section in a written plan may carry an AskUserQuestion parameter block, a Skill(...) dispatch line, or an HTML-comment directive — those stay in the skill/reference files that run the mechanics, not in `pipeline.md`'s draft template; guarded by `.github/actions/code-review-action/src/planFileOutputPurity.test.ts`, which walks the skill markdown for these constructs"
    },
    {
      "source": "docs/05-plan-run-skills.md",
      "rule": "Review-and-score is defined once in `references/pipeline.md` and executed identically by every caller (plan, run, run-primed, linear:plan) — the target score (98), the 3-pass revision budget, and any new gating behavior (e.g. a flag toggling the step) belong in that one shared file, not duplicated per-skill, so a table/threshold cannot drift from itself"
    },
    {
      "source": "docs/16-linear-plan-skill.md",
      "rule": "linear:plan diverges from plan/run/run-primed on a below-target score: it does NOT proceed on the recorded score — it reports and emits the plan to the transcript rather than storing it, because a stored plan can be executed later, unattended, by a session that never saw the score. Any change making expert review/scoring optional must preserve this asymmetry (or explicitly and visibly change it) rather than silently unifying behavior across callers"
    },
    {
      "source": "docs/16-linear-plan-skill.md",
      "rule": "`linearPlanContract.test.ts` reads the scoring threshold out of `pipeline.md` to assert one stated threshold governs every caller, and asserts the reader maps every verdict to stored-plan/fresh-plan behavior — a scoring-optionality change must keep this guard satisfiable (e.g. it needs a defined verdict/threshold state when scoring is skipped)"
    },
    {
      "source": "docs/05-plan-run-skills.md",
      "rule": "Phase 0 input detection (including its tracker gating and alert-vs-issue divergence) lives once in `references/input-detection.md`, shared verbatim by both `plan` and `linear:plan` so the tables cannot drift — a new flag parsed at Phase 0 (like `--experts-review`) belongs there, not duplicated per-skill"
    }
  ],
  "standards": [
    {
      "id": "RFC-0001",
      "title": "Reference formatting & readability",
      "status": "Accepted",
      "path": "rfc/0001-reference-formatting.md",
      "defaulted": false,
      "why": "The plan edits SKILL.md and references/*.md files (plan/pipeline.md, plan/input-detection.md, linear:plan/SKILL.md) plus docs chapters 5 and 16, all dense with skill/file/section cross-references that must stay RFC-0001-compliant, and as an Accepted RFC it is binding — a plan must not violate any of its clauses"
    }
  ],
  "dropped": [],
  "principles": [],
  "digestError": null
}
```

